# This repository is built and run entirely inside Linux containers, and its
# contents are stored with LF. Checking anything out with CRLF breaks things
# that give no hint about line endings:
#
#   *.sh  - COPYed into an image and exec'd. The shebang ends in a carriage
#           return, so the kernel looks for an interpreter literally named
#           "/bin/sh<CR>" and reports "no such file or directory" for a script
#           that is plainly there.
#   *.go  - gofmt normalises to LF, so every CRLF file counts as unformatted
#           and `golangci-lint run` fails on files nobody has touched.
#
# eol=lf therefore applies to the whole tree rather than to the two extensions
# that happened to be caught. There are no .bat/.cmd/.ps1 files here that would
# want CRLF; add an exception below if that changes.
* text=auto eol=lf
